      "answer": "$\\frac1{\\sqrt5}\\approx0.45$.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "Use the perpendicular-distance formula, or find $\\theta$ from the common gradient $\\frac12$ — M1.\n\n$\\tan\\theta=\\frac12$, so $\\theta=26.57^\\circ$ — B1.\n\n$d=\\sin(26.57^\\circ)=\\frac1{\\sqrt5}=0.45$ — A1.\n\nOR the perpendicular $y=-2x$ meets $AB$ at $\\left(\\frac15,-\\frac25\\right)$, giving $d=\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac15\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac25\\right)^2}=0.45$.\n\n[3]",
